    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a challenging slate on this July 14th afternoon, as the offense is largely neutralized by a scheduled day off for core anchors **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**. In their absence, our active rotation is forced to contend with Cease, whose 2.96 xERA represents a significant hurdle for our limited lineup. **Andy Pages** (43.41) currently serves as our strongest play, narrowly edging out **Drake Baldwin** (40.51). While **Andy Pages** benefits from the 4% park factor, the combination of his suboptimal spot in the 8-hole and the elite skill set of the opposing arm keeps his upside capped. **Drake Baldwin** remains a marginal play at best; his projection is buoyed by recent performance metrics, but he faces the same SP-skill regression as his teammates, and his position at the bottom of the order severely limits his counting stat potential.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved weighing the potential utility of **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg** against the lack of confirmed lineup data for the late games. We have opted to play it conservative with the game cap, prioritizing the preservation of our limited remaining starts over chasing marginal returns from our speed-focused specialists. While **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, we are closely monitoring the status of **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who\u2014if activated or placed in prime spots\u2014would immediately supersede the current bottom-tier options like **Brayan Rocchio** or **Curtis Mead**. Given that **Jacob Wilson**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Josh Lowe** are all currently trending below our 40-point efficiency floor, we are prepared to keep the bench locked until we see more favorable matchups for **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, and **Coby Mayo**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Lara**, and **Denzer Guzman**; should any of these players crack their respective starting lineups in high-run environments, they may serve as potential pivots to bolster our stolen base production, which remains our primary objective in the race for 5x5 dominance.",
